  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Showers, and potentially a few thunderstorms, \nlikely late this weekend into early next week.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\nA cold front approaches our area Saturday night with an area of\nlow pressure developing along it Sunday. The low should pass \nnorth of our area Sunday night into Monday. There is \nconsiderable uncertainty with the timing and strength of this \napproaching system. Guidance from the Euro has a stronger system\napproaching later Monday, while the GFS and Canadian have a \nweaker system earlier Monday. Showers and an isolated \nthunderstorm possible, mainly over northern and western Maine, \nSunday afternoon as the cold front approaches. The majority of \nthe rain is expected Monday as the low passes to our north with \nthe highest totals in north and west areas, with about a 50-60% \nchance of greater than 0.5 inches. Other areas could see up to \n0.25 inches. Uncertainty remains in the timing of the system so \nrain totals could shift or be higher in some heavier bands. Rain\ntapers off over night Monday into Tuesday. The greatest chance \nfor thunderstorms is also Monday but it is unclear how \nwidespread they will be and how far south they will extend which\nis also complicated by the timing of the system. Models are \ncurrently showing limited instability and more southerly flow \nalong the coast could bring a marine layer inland which would \ngenerally stunt convection. Fog likely each night through Sunday\nnight and may persist into the morning.",
